  "summary": "Finished the correctness guarantees of the accepted conversion design. Insertion preserves admitted content or refuses atomically; grammar validation at slice admission was prototyped and rejected because it refuses lossless fits. This corrects 2026-09-28-document-conversion-open-findings, whose claim that insertion dropped content while reporting success was a misdiagnosis: the plain-text fallback won silently. Cross-block replacement joins both boundaries into the start block; the reported trailing paragraph is the kit's TrailingBlockPlugin. The generated kit Editor proves editor parse results narrower than Value. Paste diagnostics: DataTransfer warnings declare impact, the report derives lossy, thrown format callbacks are rejected attempts, HTML and Markdown classify their warnings, the HTML decoder reports unmapped embedded content, DOMPlugin is exported, and the registry editor kit shows one toast per lossy paste. Real-browser proof exposed that mounted views missed report sinks and clipboard keys; both now resolve through the runtime owner and the projected-clipboard workaround is deleted. A createsElement mapping now creates the default block, fixing list paste in the registry kit.",
